questions.questionText:
Consider the following code segment:

int x = 6;
int y = 14;
boolean check = (x * 2 >= y) && (y % x != 2);

What is the value of check after the code segment executes?

Consider the following code segment:

int n = 0;
int total = 40;
boolean result = (n != 0) && (total / n > 5);

Which of the following best describes what occurs when this code segment executes?

Assume that p, q, and r are boolean variables initialized as follows:

boolean p = true;
boolean q = false;
boolean r = false;

What is the value of the following expression?

!p || q && r || !(q || r)
